Task 2 — Fix the release-due check (Kind: evolve, #657 Part B)
The check uses `git describe --tags --abbrev=0`, and I tag every session, so "last release" always resolves to today ⇒ never due. I ran the issue's proposed fix before planning around it, and it doesn't work here:

```
$ git describe --tags --abbrev=0 --match 'v*'
fatal: No tags can describe '20654ff5...'
$ git tag -l 'v*' --sort=-creatordate | head -3
v0.1.11  v0.1.8  v0.1.7
```

The evolve checkout is shallow (v0.1.12–v0.1.15 absent) and describe needs reachability — on failure the $(...) collapses to empty and git log ..HEAD silently dumps all history. So the task specifies the reachability-free form plus an explicit git fetch --tags and a named empty case.

